--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Provenance / derived work
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

signet-trainer is a clean-room build that harvested and ported a validated
LTX-2.3 foundation from the following projects:

1. enochiatron (private repository)
   Copyright (c) 2026 Alvdansen Labs / PromptCrafted
   Licensed under the MIT License (full text below).

   Ported: the LTX-2.3 model loader, the canonical pre-encoding path, the
   flow-matching training loop, checkpoint/resume, and the validation-gate
   discipline.

2. flimmer-trainer — Alvdansen Labs
   Copyright (c) 2026 Alvdansen Labs
   Licensed under the MIT License (full text below).

   Ported: the block-swap CPU/GPU offloader (subsequently made PEFT-LoRA-aware
   in this repository). See item 3 — that offloader has an upstream of its own.

3. musubi-tuner — kohya-ss — https://github.com/kohya-ss/musubi-tuner
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

   `src/signet_trainer/offload/block_swap.py` originated as musubi-tuner-derived
   code, reaching this repository via flimmer-trainer. The file's own header
   records that provenance.

   NOTICE OF CHANGES (Apache-2.0 §4(b)): the file has been modified from its
   upstream form. It was harvested Wan-validated rather than LTX-validated, and
   was subsequently made PEFT-LoRA-aware — `_get_linear_weights` was changed to
   descend into PEFT wrappers and enumerate every active adapter's `lora_A` /
   `lora_B` leaves, only large base weights are swapped, LoRA sub-Linears are
   kept GPU-resident, and the device guard was widened to scan all tracked
   weights. Further local changes may exist; consult the git history for the
   complete record.

   A copy of the Apache License 2.0 is included at LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

4. LTX-2 / ltx-trainer — Lightricks — https://github.com/Lightricks/LTX-2

   The LTX-2 packages (`ltx-core`, `ltx-trainer`, `ltx-pipelines`) are NOT
   vendored into this repository — the Modal GPU image git-installs them from
   the upstream repository at a pinned commit
   (`d6053703e00195bc668cbd1d5eda9dc0b2e7b74a`, recorded as `LTX2_COMMIT_SHA` in
   `src/signet_trainer/modal/app.py`).

   HOWEVER, portions of this repository are DERIVED FROM that upstream source
   and say so in their own docstrings. These are not merely "usage" — they are
   ports:

     - `src/signet_trainer/conditioning/ic_lora.py` — declares itself "a verbatim
       port of the canonical `VideoToVideoStrategy`"
       (`packages/ltx-trainer/src/ltx_trainer/training_strategies/video_to_video.py`
       at the pinned SHA), re-expressed onto this project's
       `ModelInputs` / `Modality` / `StepDeps` contract.
     - `src/signet_trainer/inference/sampler.py` — the keep-token pinning formula
       (`pin_keep_tokens`, around line 320) is declared VERBATIM the conditioning
       copy-back inside upstream `ValidationSampler._run_denoising`
       (`validation_sampler.py:571-577` at the pinned SHA); the waveform
       trim/pad helper (`_fit_waveform_to_duration`, around line 734) is declared
       VERBATIM the trim/pad of upstream
       `process_videos.VideoDataset._extract_audio` (`:194-205`).

   These portions remain subject to the upstream LTX-2 license. Consult the
   license shipped with `github.com/Lightricks/LTX-2` at the pinned commit and
   comply with it; nothing in the Signet Trainer License enlarges or restricts
   your rights in Lightricks' code.

5. diffusers — Hugging Face — https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

   `diffusers` is a declared dependency (the Modal GPU image installs it from
   git at the pinned commit `9f169d98d0bce392a889c3b6524d0d97734dfc0e`, recorded
   as `DIFFUSERS_SHA` in `src/signet_trainer/modal/app.py`), but this repository
   ALSO contains code transcribed from it:

     - `src/signet_trainer/conditioning/h3_packing.py` — the module docstring
       states it is "transcribed from diffusers" and cites, at the pinned SHA,
       `src/diffusers/modular_pipelines/minimax_h3/before_denoise.py`. The
       `patchify_video_latents` implementation (around lines 144-169) follows
       upstream `patchify_video_latents` (L44-73) line-for-line, and the RoPE
       `position_ids` construction follows the cited `_ROPE_*` constants and the
       `_spatial_position_grid` / `_temporal_position_grid` /
       `_frame_position_grid` / `_fill_audio_positions` helpers.
     - `src/signet_trainer/prep/h3_encode.py` — the video-VAE encode recipe
       (around lines 167 and 287) is declared "transcribed line-for-line from
       `encoders.py:102-136`", read at the same pinned diffusers SHA under
       `src/diffusers/modular_pipelines/minimax_h3/`; the same section carries
       the fixed keyframe-encode seed and the ImageNet pixel-normalization
       constants read from that source.

   NOTICE OF CHANGES (Apache-2.0 §4(b)): the transcribed portions have been
   modified from their upstream form — re-expressed onto this project's tensor
   contracts and payload shapes, with added validation, error messages, and
   documentation. Consult the git history for the complete record.

   A copy of the Apache License 2.0 is included at LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt.

